<%# THE VOICE ROW LAB PAGE: /profile's "Your voice" card, rendered by name with
    the test embedder as a local. What only a browser can show: the lazy
    voice-profile controller registers, the level meter moves while a take
    records, a silent take is refused, three heard takes enable Save, and Save
    posts vectors (never audio). e2e/voice_profile.spec.js drives it at phone
    width with a generated microphone, since Chrome's fake one cannot play
    chosen audio. %>
<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto py-8 px-4">
  <section class="card p-6 mb-6" data-profile-section="voice">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-heading mb-4">Your voice</h2>
    <%= render "studio/profiles/voice_section", user: @user, embedder: "fake" %>
  </section>
</div>
